A||||9||V8Fiero||Cleaning intake system?||||5||
Z||000000||V8Fiero||07-29-2001||10:44 PM||||I was tearing apart a spare 2.8 that I have and was looking at the intake system ( the three individual intakes ) and I noticed how carboned up they were. What would be a good effective way of cleaning out the carbon? I was thinking of cleaning these parts out and putting them on my 86 GT.<P>------------------<BR>86 SE Gold<BR>86 GT Red <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/RedRavensig.JPG"> <BR>"Trying to change from V8Fiero to RedRavenGT"||||reg||5
Z||000001||fiero56||07-29-2001||10:47 PM||||Carb cleaner works well. I use the stuff from AutoZone, its in a yellow can, costs 0.99 a can, works well.||||reg||1
Z||000002||AkursedX||07-30-2001||12:50 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fiero56:<BR><B>Carb cleaner works well. I use the stuff from AutoZone, its in a yellow can, costs 0.99 a can, works well.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I second that.  The stuff works wonders!!  But I'll warn you, it gets pretty messy.  <P><P>------------------<BR><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||b lo 0||07-30-2001||03:13 PM||||Carb cleaner is good, but the best stuff I've ever used is called Mean Green-it's in a pump bottle with a wierd face on it-find it at the Dollar Tree.  That stuff works on EVERYTHING!!  got stains out of my beloved Waffle House t-shirt (seriously) and proceeded to degrease the clutch pack in Mom's NX2000 in about 5 seconds, detailed the engine bay on dad's 4Runner, and got mud stains off the tires on my Jeep.  I used it to get the carbon deposits off of my throttle plate.  BTW, if you want the intake to stay clean, change the breather tube on the valve covers to a breather stack from Pep Boys or something.  That's where all the carbon comes from.  Just don't forget to plug the hole on the intake hose.<P>------------------<BR><FONT SIZE="1">'85 GT (in progress)<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.angelfire.com/ga3/audioimagery/ice.gif">      <BR>White Lightnin!  (NOT moonshine, for all you hillbillies!)</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000004||1FST2M6||07-30-2001||03:49 PM||||i lust soaked the pieces in air craft striper for a few days.  the entire thing looked brand spankin new.||||reg||1
